<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:53:30 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Four astronauts return to Earth after eight months in space</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-four-astronauts-return-to-earth-after-eight-months-in-space</link><description>
An astronaut crew that carried out an eight-month mission aboard the International Space Station splashed down as planned Thursday off the coast of California. During the mission, Sophie Adenot became the first French female astronaut to venture outside the space station for a spacewalk. In all, she undertook three spacewalks on August 18 and 25, and September 1.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4609f65e-c3ef-11f1-b71e-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261009-161312-161513-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4609f65e-c3ef-11f1-b71e-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261009-161312-161513-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4ace6a6c-c3ef-11f1-a3ef-ddfff48aed3d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:43:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Callum Turner's new film sparkles at Dinard Film Festival</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261009-callum-turner-s-new-film-sparkles-at-dinard-film-festival</link><description>
British and Irish cinema have been in the spotlight at the Breton resort of Dinard for more than three decades, with films like "The Full Monty" and "Billy Elliot" getting their starts at the town's annual film festival. FRANCE 24's Culture editor Eve Jackson brings us the latest from this year’s edition, from its line-up to the financial woes that could spell the end of the festival.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c62bc15c-c3e3-11f1-8f70-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/ARB-NEWS-09-10-2026-10-00-ING02-CLEAN-N1-frame-138700.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c62bc15c-c3e3-11f1-8f70-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/ARB-NEWS-09-10-2026-10-00-ING02-CLEAN-N1-frame-138700.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">62696ac0-c3d9-11f1-837b-87caf613bd81</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:34:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Morgane Alliot Foucaud</dc:creator></item><item><category>Scoop</category><title>Lawsuits blame Fox News for deaths of journalists in Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261009-lawsuits-blame-fox-news-for-deaths-of-journalists-in-ukraine</link><description>
This week, FRANCE 24's media show Scoop revisits a fatal assignment for a Fox News team in Ukraine. On March 14, 2022, a Russian strike hit the crew reporting near the capital Kyiv. Reporter Benjamin Hall was seriously injured and two other journalists were killed. The journalists' families are suing Fox, saying the network put the story ahead of its people. Our guest is NPR's David Folkenflik.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/df088b96-c3df-11f1-9db5-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16543625836ac8e2dae116b5-18744395.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/df088b96-c3df-11f1-9db5-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16543625836ac8e2dae116b5-18744395.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">21d41366-c3de-11f1-8f1a-ff81f5596910</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:23:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>William HILDERBRANDT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Absolute torture': Female US inmate in critical condition after botched execution</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-absolute-torture-female-us-inmate-in-critical-condition-after-botched-execution</link><description>
A condemned female murderer who survived two lethal injections during a botched execution by the US state of Tennessee was in critical condition and receiving "life-saving care," according to her attorneys. In an extraordinary chain of events, Christa Pike, 50, was whisked from a prison execution chamber to a hospital, still alive despite two deadly doses of pentobarbital. What happened to Pike is "absolute torture," said Sandrine Ageorges-Skinner, Spokesperson for Together Against the Death Penalty (ECPM), speaking to FRANCE 24's Alison Sargent.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5bbc402a-c3e9-11f1-8ce0-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261003-090459-091446-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5bbc402a-c3e9-11f1-8ce0-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261003-090459-091446-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">608cf34c-c3e9-11f1-aee0-db985a124965</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:03:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Revisited</category><title>Sierra Leone: From 'blood diamonds' to stones of hope?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261009-sierra-leone-from-blood-diamonds-to-stones-of-hopen</link><description>
"Blood diamonds" became infamous for funding the brutal civil war in Sierra Leone. Beginning 25 years ago, the Kimberley Process aimed to put an end to this illegal trade. Accused of complicity in the conflict, the diamond industry has since sought to clean up its image, emphasising an ethical shift. But a quarter of a century on, have the former "blood diamonds" truly become synonymous with development? FRANCE 24's Sarah Sakho and Simon Martin report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/76fec852-c30e-11f1-a6dc-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/billet-retour-diamant-EN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/76fec852-c30e-11f1-a6dc-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/billet-retour-diamant-EN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">562b8438-c266-11f1-b9ff-d73c73a526c3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 13:58:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Simon MARTIN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia says all clear after contact tracing in reported plague case</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-russia-says-all-clear-after-contact-tracing-in-reported-plague-case</link><description>
Russia has detected no health issues or dangerous micro-organisms after tracing all contacts of a woman who reportedly died of plague, the governor of Siberia's Irkutsk region said Thursday. Russia has not confirmed the woman died of plague, and Governor Igor Kobzev said in his statement she had contracted "community-acquired pneumonia".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9720c62c-c3e4-11f1-b067-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261009-151022-151215-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9720c62c-c3e4-11f1-b067-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261009-151022-151215-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9c31648c-c3e4-11f1-97f2-e9e0faacf421</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 13:53:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Madrid mourns evicted retiree, 'icon' of Spain housing protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-madrid-mourns-evicted-retiree-icon-of-spain-housing-protests</link><description>
Tens of thousands of mourners marched through Madrid on Thursday in tribute to a Spanish pensioner whose eviction sparked national housing protests that culminated in the calling of early elections. The death of 87-year-old Maricarmen Abascal on Wednesday produced tears and anger in the Spanish capital's emblematic Puerta del Sol square, the epicentre of the movement where hundreds are camping in protest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07660870-c3e5-11f1-8cb6-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261009-151242-151410-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07660870-c3e5-11f1-8cb6-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261009-151242-151410-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0cc5d12e-c3e5-11f1-aad2-997c946106ff</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 13:51:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>No peace without international law: The message behind Navi Pillay’s Nobel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-no-peace-without-international-law-the-message-behind-navi-pillay-s-nobel</link><description>
Navi Pillay, a South African-born jurist and former UN human rights chief whose career has spanned from defending the rights of an imprisoned Nelson Mandela to leading a panel that found that Israel committed genocide in Gaza, won the Nobel Peace Prize on Friday for her efforts to promote international law as it comes under attack. For more, FRANCE 24’s William Hilderbrandt is joined by Jørgen Watne Frydnes, Chair of the Norwegian Nobel Committee.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b438beba-c3e7-11f1-bf92-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261009-133109-133545-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b438beba-c3e7-11f1-bf92-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261009-133109-133545-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b9386afa-c3e7-11f1-83b2-453e8e78ca54</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 13:50:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French high school students react to Education Minister’s measures</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-french-high-school-students-react-to-education-minister-s-measures</link><description>
In response to the massive high school student protests in France, Education Minister Édouard Geffray announced emergency measures on Thursday, October 8. Some students reacted to these measures in interviews with France 24. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bdc298fc-c3e2-11f1-8df4-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-Reax-annonce-lyc%C3%A9es-10.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bdc298fc-c3e2-11f1-8df4-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-Reax-annonce-lyc%C3%A9es-10.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dcf0ebca-c3e2-11f1-931f-7b20d2998052</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 13:35:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Access Asia</category><title>India protests grow over Election Commission mistrust</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261009-india-protests-grow-over-election-commission-mistrust</link><description>
In this edition of Access Asia, we find out why multiple protests have broken out in India after an investigation by The Indian Express raised concerns about the integrity of the country's Election Commission. Journalist Faye D'Souza joins us to unpack how Narendra Modi's government is facing mounting pressure from the political opposition and the Gen Z-led Cockroach Janta Party. She also discusses the wider sense of discontent in India.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a141c656-c3df-11f1-ab20-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/India-protest.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a141c656-c3df-11f1-ab20-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/India-protest.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">34b9ba68-c3d8-11f1-ae80-a3a60b2bef46</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 13:08:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Joanna COCKERELL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>France’s seafood problem starts elsewhere</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20261009-france-s-seafood-problem-starts-elsewhere</link><description>
Much of the fishmeal and fish oil that support seafood consumed in France come from global supply chains linked to pollution, labour abuses, overfishing, and food insecurity in poorer countries.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf9837e4-c34d-11f1-a75d-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/main-aquaculture-v2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf9837e4-c34d-11f1-a75d-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/main-aquaculture-v2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b8a2a1f0-b19f-11f1-87cc-3900618985d3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 13:01:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf9837e4-c34d-11f1-a75d-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/main-aquaculture-v2.jpg">© Studio graphique France Médias Monde</source><dc:creator>Outlaw Ocean Project</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Morocco and Senegal await AFCON final verdict after arbitration hearing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261009-morocco-and-senegal-await-afcon-final-verdict-after-arbitration-hearing</link><description>
Thursday saw the Court of Arbitration for Sport hold a long-awaited hearing in Lausanne, as sport's highest court considered Senegal's appeal over the decision to award Morocco this year's Africa Cup of Nations title. While Senegal won the match on the pitch in Rabat 10 months ago, the Confederation of African Football later overturned the result because the Lions of Teranga had left the pitch in protest mid-game before coming back on. The three-judge panel is expected to issue a verdict soon.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c88969f4-c3a2-11f1-8c0e-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/J24-AFCON-FINAL-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c88969f4-c3a2-11f1-8c0e-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/J24-AFCON-FINAL-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3631727a-c39f-11f1-a90f-fd416716f075</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 12:59:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>No, the French army did not deploy tanks against protesting students</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261009-no-the-french-army-did-not-deploy-tanks-against-protesting-students</link><description>
France's student protests have sparked a wave of misleading content online. A viral TikTok falsely claimed the French army had deployed an armoured vehicle against protesters, when it was actually returning to a nearby military base. Other posts recycle 2023 footage of retirement protests as current events, while an AI-generated image was falsely presented as showing a police officer being attacked. Vedika Bahl examines how old, out-of-context and AI-generated content is fuelling misinformation. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3b4710ae-c3df-11f1-8541-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12738663096ac8e1c7f27161-21478823.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3b4710ae-c3df-11f1-8541-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12738663096ac8e1c7f27161-21478823.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a26889ae-c35b-11f1-acf2-e5cdbb2956f2</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 12:49:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator></dc:creator></item><item><category>The 51%</category><title>Foreign aid to Africa falls by over 25%: How women and children are bearing the brunt</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261009-foreign-aid-to-africa-falls-by-over-25-how-women-and-children-are-bearing-the-brunt</link><description>
As international aid to Africa dries up, what does it mean for women and children on the ground? We report from Kenya on the impact of cuts to US-aid backed health programmes for women. Annette Young also talks to Nana Zulu from the African Women's Development Fund on what it means for the region as a whole. Plus the bravery of Borneo's female firefighters; as Indonesia endures its worst fire season in 11 years, these women are also facing a sexist backlash.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/465d149a-c3c4-11f1-803c-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/7d98784e-a8c4-4afc-a8dd-586f8be894cc.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/465d149a-c3c4-11f1-803c-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/7d98784e-a8c4-4afc-a8dd-586f8be894cc.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">704cbb5e-c32c-11f1-b9af-b9879210c46e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 12:22:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category>Reporters</category><title>India's dowry curse: Outlawed practice remains deeply entrenched</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261009-india-dowry-curse-outlawed-practice-remains-deeply-entrenched</link><description>
India recorded 5,737 dowry-linked deaths in 2024, an average of around 16 women a day. Despite being outlawed more than six decades ago, the practice of dowry – the transfer or money or valuables from a bride's family when she gets married – remains deeply entrenched across Indian society. Our correspondents report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/71652adc-c307-11f1-92d1-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/Reporters-Inde-FR-EN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/71652adc-c307-11f1-92d1-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/Reporters-Inde-FR-EN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c41bcc3c-c333-11f1-ad89-ed1a300c4447</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 12:19:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Khansa JUNED</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Renoir paintings stolen from French Riviera museum recovered, six suspects arrested</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261009-renoir-paintings-stolen-from-french-riviera-museum-recovered-six-people-arrested</link><description>
Two ⁠Renoir paintings worth millions ​of dollars that were stolen from a ​museum on the French Riviera a month ago have been recovered and six suspects have been arrested, the ​local ‌mayor said on Friday. The thieves sliced through a fence, climbed through a window and initally stole four paintings by the French master, but abandoned two of the artworks as they fled.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/03dcaf2e-c3d6-11f1-91c8-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/60752cc446daa3d96e2dae25518a084839dfaebe.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/03dcaf2e-c3d6-11f1-91c8-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/60752cc446daa3d96e2dae25518a084839dfaebe.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4ee40950-c3da-11f1-8296-5598f45db33b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 12:09:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/03dcaf2e-c3d6-11f1-91c8-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/60752cc446daa3d96e2dae25518a084839dfaebe.jpg">© Valery Hache, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Residents of Ukraine's Kramatorsk forced to flee as drone strikes intensify</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261009-residents-of-ukraine-s-kramatorsk-forced-to-flee-as-drone-strikes-intensify</link><description>
The city of Kramatorsk, in eastern Ukraine, is increasingly coming under Russian attack. For those who have stayed behind, the threat from drones and shelling has become a daily reality. Many have resisted leaving their homes, despite the growing danger – but now, more and more residents are being forced to flee. Our colleagues at France 2 followed an evacuation from the city and witnessed first-hand the dangers that residents face.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a254ec88-c3d7-11f1-a4ce-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-14410476136ac8d50910b737-10104573.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a254ec88-c3d7-11f1-a4ce-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-14410476136ac8d50910b737-10104573.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b0984d42-c32f-11f1-937c-813a6b8358d6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 11:51:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE 2</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Eritrea and Ethiopia accuse each other of provoking war as Tigray rebels retreat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261009-eritrea-ethiopia-accuse-each-other-of-provoking-war-as-tigray-rebels-retreat</link><description>
Ethiopia and Eritrea on Friday accused each other of starting a "war of agresson" days after the two countries severed diplomatic ties. Ethiopian officals estimate that up to 8,000 Eritrean soldiers are present in Tigray supporting rebels who last month launched attacks against federal forces.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc716724-c3d5-11f1-8b99-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/278c35df4d8cae238940d8d675a1af914b2ba2a4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc716724-c3d5-11f1-8b99-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/278c35df4d8cae238940d8d675a1af914b2ba2a4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bd0756d0-c3d5-11f1-b959-09f43b7eeaf1</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 11:36:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc716724-c3d5-11f1-8b99-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/278c35df4d8cae238940d8d675a1af914b2ba2a4.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Navi Pillay wins the Nobel Peace Prize for her work in international justice</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-navi-pillay-wins-the-nobel-peace-prize-for-her-work-in-international-justice</link><description>
The South African-born jurist and former UN human rights chief Navi Pillay, who is currently an ad hoc judge at the International Court of Justice, won the Nobel Peace Prize on Friday for her efforts to promote peace and international law. Her win is sure to be seen as a high-profile rebuke to US President Trump and Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, who have both rejected the findings of a UN commission she led that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. Both leaders also have been highly critical of the institutions where Pillay has worked. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6cac4412-c3d4-11f1-a6c5-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261009-130106-130719-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6cac4412-c3d4-11f1-a6c5-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261009-130106-130719-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7168e5c8-c3d4-11f1-84cd-4bf401ee3651</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 11:31:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'The Blue Fighter': Zimbabwean author Kundizeza wins 2026 Caine Prize</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-the-blue-fighter-zimbabwean-writer-kundizeza-wins-2026-caine-prize</link><description>
A big win for Zimbabwean literature: Harare-based author Simbarashe Steyn Kundizeza has claimed the 2026 Caine Prize for African Writing for his short story "The Blue Fighter". The award is given to the best short story by an African writer published in English and comes with a £10,000 pounds cash prize. FRANCE 24's Sharon Mazingaizo met with the writer.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7e3bba88-c3d3-11f1-b5d8-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-215608-215723-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7e3bba88-c3d3-11f1-b5d8-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-215608-215723-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">838fc998-c3d3-11f1-a902-fd259d60e1e2</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 11:27:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Senegal, Morocco to get AFCON title verdict within days</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-senegal-morocco-to-get-afcon-title-verdict-within-days</link><description>
The Court of Arbitration for Sport (CAS) on Thursday opened its hearing into Senegal's appeal against being stripped of the Africa Cup of Nations (AFCON) title in favour of Morocco. The hearing in Lausanne comes almost 10 months after Pape Gueye's extra-time goal gave Senegal victory over the tournament hosts following a chaotic finish to normal time. But in March, the Confederation of African Football (CAF) overturned that result, awarding Morocco a 3-0 victory, and the title.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ba25396-c3d1-11f1-95dd-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-214500-214651-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ba25396-c3d1-11f1-95dd-ef6152f87623/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-214500-214651-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">90dfccee-c3d1-11f1-a738-41688afbb9e9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 11:25:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Kenya Red Cross supports response to country’s first Ebola case</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-kenya-red-cross-supports-response-to-country-s-first-ebola-case</link><description>
A Kenyan national who had been living in Congo before returning to Nairobi has become Kenya’s first confirmed Ebola case and the country’s first fatality from the disease in the rapidly evolving outbreak. The Kenya Red Cross is supporting the government’s efforts to prevent a public health crisis. FRANCE 24’s Bastien Renouil met with Paul Olala, the NGO’s head of health security and emergencies.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d72f1fbe-c3d2-11f1-961a-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-214727-215043-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d72f1fbe-c3d2-11f1-961a-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-214727-215043-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dc9a1b98-c3d2-11f1-ab35-bf71fce1cc7f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 11:24:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ebola outbreak: Border surveillance gaps raise concerns in the Central African Republic</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-ebola-outbreak-border-surveillance-gaps-raise-concerns-in-the-central-african-republic</link><description>
The fight against Ebola poses a challenge in the Central African Republic. In Zemio, in the country’s south-east, proximity to the Democratic Republic of Congo has raised fears that the virus could spread across the border. But health screening remains difficult. The repeated absence of health workers at checkpoints is hampering surveillance, while residents continue to cross the border through unofficial crossing points, as FRANCE 24's team on the ground reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53d9dcc0-c3d3-11f1-b2d8-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-215111-215259-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53d9dcc0-c3d3-11f1-b2d8-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261008-215111-215259-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">58eb22f0-c3d3-11f1-bb60-fbf83c8ec8c4</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 11:23:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pentagon vows to livestream first military execution in decades</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261009-pentagon-vows-to-livestream-first-military-execution-in-decades</link><description>
The first US military execution in more than 65 years will be livestreamed, announced the Pentagon on Thursday, after Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth said it would be "public".
 
Former Army psychiatrist Nidal Hasan opened fire at Fort Hood in Texas in 2009, killing 13 people. His execution will take place at the military base on December 3, 2026.
 
 "The livestreaming of an execution is tantamount to a public execution and would breach the absolute prohibition of torture," the Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights said on Friday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7d18288-c3ca-11f1-98a3-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/Nidal-Hasan-execution00.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7d18288-c3ca-11f1-98a3-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/Nidal-Hasan-execution00.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fcb4c3ae-c3ca-11f1-a485-5fede210fc06</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 10:56:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
